<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">C. P. Ramaswami Iyer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1879">1879</a>–<a href="/years/1966">1966</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">C. P. Ramaswami Iyer was an Indian lawyer and administrator who served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diwan">diwan</a> of Travancore from 1936 to 1947. He backed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-entry-proclamation">Temple Entry Proclamation</a> of 1936, expanded industry and education, and founded the University of Travancore. In 1947 he declared that Travancore would become independent rather than join <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, but after protests and an attempt on his life he resigned, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> acceded to India.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/c-p-ramaswami-iyer.jpg" alt="C. P. Ramaswami Iyer" width="239" height="350" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Hindu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CPRamaswami_Aiyar_1939.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
